<!--
  ic_bar_more — reader bar, dot-matrix set.

  Three rules, five dots each. It was three dots in a row, which is the same glyph the
  bar used to set in type and carries the same problem at this size: three marks on one
  line read as punctuation left behind rather than as a control. Three lines read as a
  menu, which is what the panel behind it is.

  Five glyphs on one 7x7 lattice of identical dots: pitch 1.5, radius 0.55, first center
  at 1.5, inside a 12x12 viewport. Every glyph is centered on (6,6), which is the half of
  this that is not decoration — the bar used to hold one icon from light-sdk, two drawn
  here and a row of text, each with its own padding and its own idea of where the middle
  was, so none of them sat on the same line.

  Nothing is stroked and nothing is scaled. A glyph is only ever which dots are lit, so
  the set cannot drift: a new one is a new dot map and it lines up by construction.

  White, and tinted where it is used. The bar is white over a letter and black over plain
  text, and one file serves both.
-->
